DOCKERFILE DESIGN PRINCIPLE (BUILD ONCE, PASS ARTIFACT TO DOCKER):
The CI/CD pipeline compiles the application binaries in prior build steps. The Dockerfile MUST be a clean, minimal runtime container that consumes these pre-compiled build artifacts. Do NOT include heavy SDK/compilation stages or dependency restoration steps inside the Dockerfile.

STRUCTURE & RULES:
   - For `static_frontend`: Use `nginx:alpine` as base image. Remove default NGINX content with `RUN rm -rf /usr/share/nginx/html/*`. Copy pre-built static web assets from `{{ artifact_path }}` directly into NGINX document root `/usr/share/nginx/html/` (use trailing slash, e.g. `COPY {{ artifact_path }}/ /usr/share/nginx/html/`). EXPOSE port 80, and set CMD to `["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]`.
